archmage84 wrote:
> I should probably mention a few things about my playing style:
> 6. I've never entered the Quest.
Especially for wizard and valk, do so before diving for the castle.
Both quest artifacts are worth getting early.  Kick sinks and
foocubus dance for the last few levels.

> 7. I've never hit the Castle, yet I long to do so.
Don't worry about that yet.  One thing at a time.  Some people do
advocate a controlled dive for the castle wand, but I like a more
conservative approach.  Clear each level so you have somewhere to
run away to.

> 8. I #twoweapon like crazy once I can.
> 9. I know about the skill stuff too, so don't worry about that.
Good.

> 10. Artifacts I want to get are in this order:
>  a) Eyes of the Overworld - wish
>  b) Greyswandir - wish
>  c) PYEC - wish
>  d) Mjollnir - sacrifest
>  e) Orb of Fate - quest
Personally, I'd put the Eye of the Aethiopica at the top of that list.
MR, half spell damage (less useful once you get the Orb as well), and
the branchport lets you escape straight to your stash whenever you 
want (as long as you wait until it's recharged before heading back
into dangerous territory.)  And you don't even need to equip it for
any of this.  It's always my first wish if I don't have too many
artifacts already.  I even prefer it over SDSM.


> 11. My desired setup is as follows (forgive the incorrect syntax where
> necessary):
>  Weapons
>  a - the blessed +7 Grayswandir (weapon in hand)
>  b - a blessed +7 silver saber (wielded in other hand)
>  Armour
That's ideal, but take what you can get.  Grayswandir will probably
require a wish for a neutral character, and Frostbrand or Mojo will
work fine.

>  c - a +5 Hawaiian shirt
>  d - a +5 silver dragon scale mail
>  e - a +5 oilskin cloak
>  d - a +5 gauntlets of power
>  e - a +5 helm of telepathy
>  f - a +5 boots of speed
I prefer a cloak of MR over oilskin (just put the oilskin on
when you're in Water; you can reliably avoid eels everywhere
else.)  A couple monsters (e.g. Rodney) can steal your quest
artifact, so have another source of MR.

The rest is good, but again, don't be too picky about
the gauntlets and helmet.  Once you've eaten all the giants
from the quest, all the gauntlets are good for is throwing Mojo,
and the helm isn't really worth a wish.  But enchanting everything
to +4 or +5 is definitely good.

>  Rings
>  g - a blessed ring of slow digestion (worn on right hand)
>  h - a blessed ring of conflict
>  i - a blessed +x ring of increase damage (worn on left hand)
>  j - a blessed +x ring of increase damage
If you're two-weaponing, the ring of increase damage is superfluous.
Use free action instead.  Don't worry about maximizing damage output;
work on minimizing the possibility of something going so wrong you
can't run away.  Slow digestion becomes less useful after you get
all the food rations from the castle soldiers, but it's nice for
the midgame and Famine.  Add levitate to the list, but don't wear
it normally.

>  Amulets
>  k - a blessed amulet of life saving (worn around neck)
>  k - a blessed amulet of magical breathing
Good choice.  You can find "LS in Vlad's tower, so if you
don't have one by the time you reach the Valley, consider a
controlled dive for it.

I'd also add some miscellaneous items:
blessed unicorn horn
blessed luckstone
blessed scroll of genocide //if you can't get away from a monster
cursed scroll of teleport //escape item
2-3 blessed potions of full healing
5-10 +6 daggers or 100 blessed +6 poison darts
oilskin sack:
    blessed scroll of remove curse //for uncursing BoH
Bag of holding:
    many rations
    more daggers or darts
    more potions of healing
    tinning kit
    pickaxe

And of course as much as you can carry, but these are the ones
that spring immediately to mind.


